From 2c6cc7e7742ee9c2fc14437dd023ebbae1bbecc0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zach Sailer <zsailer@apple.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:04:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Build test requests with an explicit start line

Tornado 6.6 deprecates passing method, uri and version to
HTTPServerRequest, and 6.7 will require start_line. With warnings turned
into errors, every test that builds a request that way fails.

- Add an http_request helper in tests/utils.py that builds the request with
  a RequestStartLine
- Use it in the base handler, websocket and allow-origin tests, the kernel
  connection tests and the gateway tests
---
 tests/base/test_allow_origin_pat.py       |  8 ++++----
 tests/base/test_handlers.py               | 22 +++++++++++-----------
 tests/base/test_websocket.py              |  4 ++--
 tests/services/kernels/test_connection.py |  6 +++---
 tests/test_gateway.py                     |  8 ++++----
 tests/utils.py                            | 10 ++++++++++
 6 files changed, 34 insertions(+), 24 deletions(-)

